  },
  {
   "id": "dcn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 796,
   "y": 672,
   "width": 157,
   "height": 16,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100056,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700392,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "price is an INTEGER",
   "originalText": "price is an INTEGER",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dcd2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 796,
   "y": 694,
   "width": 688,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100057,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700399,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "float cannot represent decimal prices exactly, and a price comparison is what decides\nwhether two orders MATCH - so a representation error is a WRONG MATCH, not a rounding error.",
   "originalText": "float cannot represent decimal prices exactly, and a price comparison is what decides\nwhether two orders MATCH - so a representation error is a WRONG MATCH, not a rounding error.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dc3",
   "type": "ellipse",
   "x": 770,
   "y": 730,
   "width": 12,
   "height": 12,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e40af",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100058,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700406,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "dcn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 796,
   "y": 730,
   "width": 237,
   "height": 16,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100059,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700413,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "the timestamp is stamped ONCE",
   "originalText": "the timestamp is stamped ONCE",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dcd3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 796,
   "y": 752,
   "width": 666,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100060,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700420,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "no component downstream ever reads a clock: a clock read inside the loop would break both\nthe budget and functional determinism. It travels with the event, so replay uses it.",
   "originalText": "no component downstream ever reads a clock: a clock read inside the loop would break both\nthe budget and functional determinism. It travels with the event, so replay uses it.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 668,
   "width": 761,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100061,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700427,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And what the sequence number does that a timestamp cannot: it IS the definition of priority.\nTwo orders arriving in the same nanosecond still have distinct sequence numbers, so price-time\npriority is always unambiguous. Timestamps have resolution limits and clock skew; a monotonic\ninteger from a single writer has neither.",
   "originalText": "And what the sequence number does that a timestamp cannot: it IS the definition of priority.\nTwo orders arriving in the same nanosecond still have distinct sequence numbers, so price-time\npriority is always unambiguous. Timestamps have resolution limits and clock skew; a monotonic\ninteger from a single writer has neither.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
