   "versionNonce": 701176,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Where the guarantees go - and the inversion that buys the latency",
   "originalText": "Where the guarantees go - and the inversion that buys the latency",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1802,
   "width": 971,
   "height": 178,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100169,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701183,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "order books (in-memory)  SERIAL, single-threaded    one thread owns them, so no consistency model is needed at all - the\n                                                    ABSENCE OF CONCURRENCY is the guarantee\nevent stream             TOTALLY ORDERED, 1 writer  the sequencer is the only writer, so the order is unambiguous by\n                                                    construction. This IS the definition of what happened.\nstandby engine state     BYTE-IDENTICAL to primary  not 'eventually consistent' - identical, which is what makes\n                                                    promotion safe\nreporting store          EVENTUAL, seconds behind   lag is fine for reporting; a GAP is a compliance incident, so\n                                                    completeness is monitored even though freshness is not\nmarket data store        EVENTUAL, sub-second       rebuilt independently by the publisher, which doubles as a\n                                                    cross-check on engine correctness\npositions                EVENTUAL, recomputed       intraday estimates for risk; authoritative at end-of-day settlement",
   "originalText": "order books (in-memory)  SERIAL, single-threaded    one thread owns them, so no consistency model is needed at all - the\n                                                    ABSENCE OF CONCURRENCY is the guarantee\nevent stream             TOTALLY ORDERED, 1 writer  the sequencer is the only writer, so the order is unambiguous by\n                                                    construction. This IS the definition of what happened.\nstandby engine state     BYTE-IDENTICAL to primary  not 'eventually consistent' - identical, which is what makes\n                                                    promotion safe\nreporting store          EVENTUAL, seconds behind   lag is fine for reporting; a GAP is a compliance incident, so\n                                                    completeness is monitored even though freshness is not\nmarket data store        EVENTUAL, sub-second       rebuilt independently by the publisher, which doubles as a\n                                                    cross-check on engine correctness\npositions                EVENTUAL, recomputed       intraday estimates for risk; authoritative at end-of-day settlement",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1090,
   "y": 1802,
   "width": 568,
   "height": 162,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100170,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 701190,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The asymmetry worth naming: the strongest guarantee in the system -\ntotal order, single writer - applies to an append-only stream in\nVOLATILE shared memory, while every DURABLE store is an eventually-\nconsistent projection.\n\nThat inverts the usual arrangement, where the durable store is\nauthoritative and caches lag behind it - and it is exactly what buys\nthe latency. The trade is that a total power loss with a\nsimultaneously-dead standby loses in-flight events, which is accepted,\nand is the reason the standby is HOT rather than warm.",
   "originalText": "The asymmetry worth naming: the strongest guarantee in the system -\ntotal order, single writer - applies to an append-only stream in\nVOLATILE shared memory, while every DURABLE store is an eventually-\nconsistent projection.\n\nThat inverts the usual arrangement, where the durable store is\nauthoritative and caches lag behind it - and it is exactly what buys\nthe latency. The trade is that a total power loss with a\nsimultaneously-dead standby loses in-flight events, which is accepted,\nand is the reason the standby is HOT rather than warm.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
